Feature: MACD, Heikin-Ashi & Channel Showcase
  Primary timeframe: 1d
  Parameter atr_period default 14
  Parameter vol_period default 20

  # Showcase demo (NOT profit-tuned): MACD as numeric series (macd_line /
  # macd_signal / macd_histogram) AND as cross primitives, the remaining HA
  # primitives (ha_doji, ha_strong), the highest_close / lowest_close channel,
  # avg_volume, and an atr_value stop.

  Background:
    Given a series macd defined as macd_line(12, 26, 9)
    And a series signal defined as macd_signal(12, 26, 9)
    And a series hist defined as macd_histogram(12, 26, 9)
    And a series hi defined as highest_close(20)
    And a series lo defined as lowest_close(20)
    And a series avg_vol defined as avg_volume(vol_period)

  Scenario: Enter long on a MACD line/signal cross with a positive histogram and volume
    Given no open position
    When macd crosses above signal
    And hist is above 0
    And volume is above avg_vol
    Then long_entry
    And with stop_loss at entry_price - 2 * atr_value(atr_period)

  Scenario: Enter long on a strong bullish Heikin-Ashi candle inside the channel
    Given no open position
    When ha_strong_bullish()
    And close is below hi
    Then long_entry
    And with stop_loss at entry_price - 2 * atr_value(atr_period)

  Scenario: Exit long on a MACD bearish cross
    Given a long position is open
    When macd_bearish_cross()
    Then long_exit

  Scenario: Exit long on a Heikin-Ashi doji
    Given a long position is open
    When ha_doji()
    Then long_exit

  Scenario: Enter short on a MACD line/signal cross down with a negative histogram
    Given no open position
    When macd crosses below signal
    And hist is below 0
    And close is above lo
    Then short_entry
    And with stop_loss at entry_price + 2 * atr_value(atr_period)

  Scenario: Exit short on a MACD bullish cross
    Given a short position is open
    When macd_bullish_cross()
    Then short_exit

  Scenario: Exit short on any strong Heikin-Ashi candle
    Given a short position is open
    When ha_strong()
    Then short_exit
